  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea - Australian Policing Partnership (PNG-APP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Papua New Guinea Australia Policing Partnership is a partnership between the Royal Papua New Guinea Constabulary (RPNGC) and the Australian Federal Police (AFP) which has been established through collaboration and commitment towards achieving shared policing outcomes. The RPNGC and AFP collaboratively identify areas of support for their policing priorities and then work together to achieve these outcomes. Support includes areas such as corporate reform, and the uplift of core policing and operational capability. Working together to strengthen Pacific police forces helps support peace, security and prosperity across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
